                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/5264: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-05-05T20:00:00+08:00">May 5, 1930—8 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 8—10:40 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>306. Legation’s 299, May 2, 5 p.m. Under instructions from the Inspector General
                    the Commissioner of Customs at Tientsin on May 3 directed the Customs Bank to
                    turn over to him balance of all customs funds on hand. The bank declined,
                    pleading “force majeure”. The Commissioner of Customs is from today both
                    assessing and collecting customs duties on behalf of the Central Government.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
